1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Modern developers use more than one AI coding agent,
but every CLI has separate projects, sessions, and workflows.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Fragmentation creates too many windows, scattered history,
constant context switching, and difficult comparisons.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Parallel Agents brings every workflow into one focused,
project-first desktop experience.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Electron, an isolated IPC bridge, project and session discovery,
and PTY runtimes create a secure, modular architecture.

5
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:55,000
One session resumes automatically. Multiple sessions clearly
guide the developer to choose the right history.

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Switch faster, see projects clearly, preserve continuity,
reduce cognitive load, and improve multi-agent productivity.

7
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Projects and sessions stay on the left, agents run in dedicated tabs,
and Explorer plus Git keep the complete workflow visible.

8
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Parallel Agents: one reliable workspace
for the way developers actually use AI today.
